WEBVTT

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.520
It's so hot!

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.620
I'm gonna melt.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:08.280
I want some ice cream.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.180
Nope. Curry.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:11.620
Why?

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.530
And so,

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.820
since our midterms are over,

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:22.620
I've used the funds we've acquired to place 
an order for TABs, tree attachment bolts.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Secret Hideout (Tree House)

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Work Progress Checklist

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Responsible Party

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Hikage Takumi

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Yasaku

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Yasaku

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
(Yasaku family)

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Serufu

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Hikage Takumi

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Task

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Collect money

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Order TAB (tree attachment bolts)

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Gather scrap materials

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Design concept image

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.630
Map layout

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:27.280
Early next week, starting Monday after school, 
I'd like to start work on the secret hideout.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.700
As a quick overview, for the first week,

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.980
we'll be doing things like cutting 
lumber and knotting rope. Prep work.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.700
Leave all of the heavy lifting to me!

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.640
If we're missing any tools or components, 
we'll get them ready during that time.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.620
The next week, we'll be installing the TABs.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.370
We'll build footholds, the 
foundation, and the floor.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:49.650
I see.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.230
After that, we'll combine our strengths...

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.570
and put our secret hideout together!

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:58.080
I'm super excited, meow!

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.090
Let's go, everyone! Do it...

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.960
yourself!

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:38.260
Serufu, how were the 
results of your midterms?

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.770
Oh! I placed third!

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.250
Wh-What?!

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.600
<b>Step 9
Does "DIY" Mean a Shocking Surprise? How Unexpected! It's Really Unexpected!</b>

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.320
Third?

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:50.150
In your class?

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.640
From the bottom?

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:54.810
In my grade. From the top.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.200
W-Wow...

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.470
You're surprisingly intelligent.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.440
Serufu-san was originally planning 
on going to YuuVoc, right?

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.120
Really?

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.450
But I didn't get in.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:11.490
Oh, but Takumin is even more amazing!

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.310
She was first in our grade!

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:14.330
Yes...

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.200
F-First?!

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.710
<b>First in                                        Her Grade</b>

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.080
It's just by chance!

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.480
Just by chance, I happened to get 
a perfect score in most subjects!

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.910
By chance...

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.870
in most of her subjects... 
she got a perfect score?

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.830
What are these power words she speaks?

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.660
B-But, Serufu-san, if you hadn't 
fallen asleep during the test,

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.550
your scores would have been 
even better, wouldn't they?

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.970
I was a little tired.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.800
Why are you acting shy?

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.620
Well, it's okay, right?

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.350
I have no idea.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.410
What about you, Jobko?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.220
Fourth.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.880
I never imagined that Serufu would beat me.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:54.410
Y-You guys are amazing.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.990
Every score other than Japanese was perfect!

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.960
<b>Yuu
Girls'</b>

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.960
<b>Gata
Girls'</b>

00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.720
Oh, right.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:03.470
You mentioned that reading and writing 
in Japanese is still difficult for you.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.000
I don't have problems reading it anymore!

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.090
Writing it is hard.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:14.170
<b>Yua Serufu</b>

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:15.230
<b>Hikage Takumi</b>

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:15.230
<b>Jobko</b>

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:12.610
Honestly! Japan has 
hiragana, katakana, kanji...

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:15.230
<b>Kouki Kokoro</b>

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:15.220
That's way too many ways of writing stuff!

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:20.030
And why, in this paperless era, would 
anyone use a handwritten answer sheet?

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:22.470
There isn't any air conditioning 
in the classrooms...

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.580
and voting in elections 
is done on paper, too!

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.630
How is this an advanced nation?!

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.000
Voting has nothing to do with this, does it?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.140
YuuVoc has air conditioning 
and our tests are paperless.

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.200
It's common sense!

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.330
Shii, are your test results...

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.380
But the fact that you got into YuuVoc 
means that you get good grades, right?

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.140
They're not really that great!

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.410
Leadercchi, how did your grades turn out?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.880
They're not bad.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.530
How good is "not bad"?

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.070
"Not bad" means "not bad."

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:05.290
Well, let's leave the 
discussion of grades here.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:07.870
Then, since all our midterms are over...

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.370
We just need to go to Serufu's house, right?

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.880
Yes! Exactly!

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.120
Then, let's meet up this Sunday at 1 PM!

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:29.180
If only it were downhill both ways...

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.870
So, you're acting like 
it's all super important,

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.570
but what is it that you want to show us?

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:38.810
That's something to look forward to.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:47.670
Serufu, every night I hear...

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:51.520
the sounds of sawing and banging
 and pounding until really late.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.010
Saw
Saw

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.990
Bang
Bang

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:51.990
Bam
Bam

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.390
It's connected, right?

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.670
You heard?!

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:59.380
How could I not hear sounds that loud?

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.640
And you've got more injuries than before.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:05.330
Pudding was worried about you, too.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.590
Purin was?

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.830
Why are you acting shy?

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.130
Oh, I know!

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:13.880
I should have Purin come, too!

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.940
Okay! And, send!

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:19.400
Huh?

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.360
My bicycle has fallen over.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:24.550
Dear, oh dear.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.360
Let's see.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.730
If I'm right...

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:31.530
There it is!

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:33.530
<b>Meat's House</b>

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.920
Back when Meat had only 
just come to our home...

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:41.690
I thought it would be sad if he didn't 
have his own house, so I made one, but...

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:42.630
Stab

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:48.650
The straw was prickly, so I think 
I remember that he just kept crying.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:00.520
Ow, ow, ow...

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:03.820
She really is such a klutz.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:21.330
Today

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:21.330
Come to my house tomorrow at 1 PM~☆ 
There's something I want to show you♡ 
Everyone from the DIY club is coming, too~♪

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:21.330
What is it you want to show me?

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:21.330
That's something to look forward to seeing 
once you get here~

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:18.840
<i>Come to my house tomorrow at 1 PM!</i>

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:21.270
<i>There's something I want to show you</i>

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.710
<i>Everyone from the DIY club is coming, too!</i>

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:35.970
What could she possibly be 
trying to accomplish?

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:38.580
Well... Maybe a pig's—

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:39.730
Simmered for pork kakuni?!

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:43.220
A pig's house. Or maybe a 
house for a cat or a dog.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:49.100
Basically, she wants to prove that she can 
be useful in building the secret hideout.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:50.230
Why?

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:54.390
The accessories that Serufu made 
haven't sold at all, right?

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:59.360
So she thinks that she's the only 
one who hasn't been any help.

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:01.230
I think that's what she's feeling.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:02.890
I see.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:06.730
But it's not like she 
needs to worry about it.

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:13.030
Serufu has fantastical and bizarre 
ideas that no one else has!

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:18.510
So she should just leave the things she 
can't do to me... to someone else!

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:22.030
"Live and let live." 
That's what you mean, right?

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:25.940
Pudding, you really are Serufu's 
best friend, aren't you?

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.020
What?!

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.280
<i>Stare...</i>

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:33.160
Wh-Why are you looking at me like that?

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:37.150
It might be better to be a little more 
honest about your feelings, don't you think?

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:41.050
No one asked for your advice!

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:46.230
No!

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:50.050
You got shampoo in my eyes! 
Time for a counterattack!

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:50.790
Bath towel. Bath towel.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.530
H-Hey! Stop that right now!

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:57.140
Lovely maidens bathing amiably...

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.270
Ah, how elegant!

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:05.090
Come in!

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:08.220
Welcome to the Yua home!

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:11.570
Welcome, DIY club!

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:14.750
Thank you for always looking 
after my daughter!

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.400
Even though I'm not much good at anything.

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:20.550
Hello, I'm the club leader, Yasaku Rei.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.030
Thank you for having us, I'm Hikage Takumi.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:29.180
I'm Kouki Kokoro! And I'm 
also Suridecchi's classmate!

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:32.130
Oh, my! Are you?

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.180
Purin-chan, Jobko-chan, welcome to you, too.

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:38.250
Oh! Yes, thank you for having us.

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:40.690
Thank you for inviting me.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.930
Well then, will you show us now, Serufu?

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:47.260
Yes! Everyone, we are 
heading to the backyard!

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.400
Ta-dah!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:59.450
And now, I will make a pig's house!

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.790
It's exactly like you said 
when we were in the bath.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.000
Bingo!

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:08.490
That lumber. Did you cut it 
all to size yourself, Serufu?

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:09.460
Yes!

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:10.980
No way!

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:14.790
So that's why you kept getting 
so many more scrapes, meow.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:18.090
Is this also the reason why you
 fell asleep during our midterms?

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:20.670
Honestly.

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:26.040
How can you focus more on a pig's house 
than on something as important as midterms?

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:29.270
I will put this pig's house 
together perfectly...

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:33.830
because I want to prove that I can be 
useful in building our secret hideout!

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.450
That's right.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:37.310
Right?

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:40.020
"Be useful"?

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:42.320
Even if you didn't do all this...

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:44.120
And now!

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:46.630
I shall begin!

00:10:46.630 --> 00:10:49.330
Hey. Don't wave tools around.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.840
Y-Yes, ma'am! I'm sorry.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:56.900
Yua Serufu...

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:59.960
do it yourself!

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:13.550
Oh... They're all different lengths.

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:16.980
If I make this one a little shorter...

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:21.050
No, maybe this one needs 
to be a little longer...

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:30.070
I forgot to change the rotation 
direction on the driver!

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:33.670
This seems like it'll take a while.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:38.170
Okay. I think that'll be okay now.

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:41.290
Should we all make something, too?

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:42.640
Yes, let's.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.940
And there's a whole bunch of lumber here.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:48.020
What do you think about a scratching post?

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:51.370
Yeah? It'd make you happy?

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.930
Okay then, leave it to me!

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:58.420
Let's see. Maybe we'll make 
a stand for your food.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:03.960
There's no point in just sitting around.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:05.460
Right?

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:08.570
That's true.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:16.560
Okay. Takumicchi, could you hold this 
for me so that the pole stays straight?

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:17.750
Will do!

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:24.260
Is this about the right height?

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.840
A little taller might be better.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:31.280
That looks incredibly precarious...

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:36.100
Will you be able to 
finish that today... Serufu?

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:38.350
Don't worry, Purin!

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:42.620
I'm gonna make you a 
really cool house, Meat!

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:48.830
Everyone, you've all been working so hard!

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.990
I've cut up some watermelon,
 so why don't we all take a break now?

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:54.860
Eat it while it's still cold, all right?

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:56.670
Thank you!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.870
Thank you, Serufu's mom!

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:05.660
You can do it, Serufu!

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:16.140
The watermelon's so sweet! 
It's bringing me back to life!

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.060
The roasted barley tea is delicious!

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.890
Right, Takumicchi?

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:21.970
Yes! I can feel it spreading 
through my whole body.

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:26.980
Coke mixed with roasted 
barley tea. I like it!

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.440
Still...

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:39.100
It seems a little... crooked.

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:42.280
Well, I guess it's okay.

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:45.530
It's not okay?

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:49.700
Oh, all right. I'll fix it.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:53.590
If I make this side shorter...

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.590
She's having a tough time of it, meow.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.880
No, making the other side 
longer would be better.

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:55.760
Serufu-san...

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:57.690
It's hard to watch, right?

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.690
<b>Ears</b>

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:04.190
<b>Tail</b>

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:07.820
Man, this makes me nervous.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:12.960
This indented part marks where 
the jigsaw's blade goes,

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:12.950
<b>This</b>

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:16.450
so I'll align that with 
the lines of the drawing.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:20.470
When the blade come into contact 
with the board it'll jump hard,

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.380
<b>This separation</b>

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.380
<b>is important</b>

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:24.090
so it's important to start 
with it away from the board.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:33.730
Serufu!

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:43.590
Let me see it?

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:45.120
What? But...

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.980
I wanted to show you that 
I can do it myself.

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:49.320
What are you talking about?

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:55.830
In the DIY club, we're a team, right?

00:14:58.070 --> 00:15:01.100
Serufu-san, let's build it together!

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:02.370
No need to force it.

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:05.410
Everyone should just do what they can, meow!

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:09.900
But the accessories I made haven't sold...

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:11.770
and I'm not very useful...

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:14.850
<b>Useless</b>

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:14.850
<b>Clumsy</b>

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:13.270
and I'm clumsy...

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:14.670
Don't worry.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:19.900
Serufu, you're the only one who can 
come up with the ideas that you do, right?

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:21.530
That's more than enough!

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:27.180
That's what Pudding said.

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:27.990
Wha?!

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:30.490
Purin said that?

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:35.910
I-I think that being able to 
come up with unique ideas...

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.990
is one of the good things about you, Serufu.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:46.520
Serufu, you're not useless at all.

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:49.850
So, come on, let me see that jigsaw.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:52.860
Yes, ma'am!

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.870
Thank you for your help.

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:57.530
Good. Just like that.

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:00.170
Then, starting again...

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.900
Do it...

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:05.470
yourself!

